## 🔧 Development Workflow

### 1. Planning Phase
- Review [Architecture](mdc:architecture.mdc) for project structure
- Plan feature using Clean Architecture principles

### 2. Implementation Phase
- Use [Riverpod](mdc:riverpod.mdc) for state management
- Implement UI with [UI Components](mdc:ui_components.mdc)
- Apply [Responsive](mdc:responsive.mdc) patterns
- Add [Internationalization](mdc:i18n.mdc) support
- Implement [Error Handling](mdc:error_handling.mdc)
- Follow [Performance](mdc:performance.mdc) guidelines
- Use [Flutter](mdc:flutter.mdc) best practices

### 3. Testing Phase
- Write tests following [Testing](mdc:testing.mdc) patterns
- Test all functionality and edge cases
- Verify performance requirements

### 4. Review Phase
- Ensure all rules are followed
- Check for consistency across the codebase
- Verify test coverage

## 🎯 Key Principles

### 1. Clean Architecture
- Clear separation of concerns
- Dependency inversion
- Single responsibility principle

### 2. Human-Centered Design
- Speed above all (≤9s expense entry)
- Cultural intelligence (local numerals, languages)
- Empathetic error messages and feedback
- No shame, no judgment in UI/UX

### 3. Performance First
- Const constructors everywhere
- Optimized rebuilds with Riverpod
- Responsive design patterns
- Offline-first architecture

### 4. Cultural Intelligence
- Bengali-first interface design
- Local payment method integration
- Festival and cultural event awareness
- Regional spending pattern recognition

### 5. Maintainability
- Comprehensive testing
- Clear documentation
- Consistent patterns

### 6. Accessibility
- Semantic labels
- Screen reader support
- Internationalization
- Cultural accessibility (RTL support, local fonts)

